            <ArticleTitle>Pain Management: Strategies for Screening and Monitoring Patients Receiving Chronic Opioid Therapy .</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>669-672</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1188/17.CJON.669-672</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The current state of pain management within the oncology setting, effectiveness of opioids for the relief of pain, and limited alternatives for chronic pain management have produced reliance on opioid medications with an inherent risk for aberrant behavior. Although standardization is lacking among prescribers who manage cancer-related pain, advanced practice RNs must act according to the available evidence that suggests assessing and monitoring for abuse and misuse.  .</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
